{{~##
   One abstract type and its variants. `structure` is the single declaration this file is for.

   **Classes and `is_a?`.** Like Python this language has inheritance, so it is not in section
   7's third group either - the shape C# takes reads naturally here.

   The read path is untouched: the file is still read into the table's flat entry and the value
   is built from it. spec/polymorphism.md section 7.
##~}}
{{ include 'ruby-file-head.sbn' ~}}
  # One value of +{{ structure.name }}+, whichever shape it took.
  #
  # Narrow it with +is_a?+.
  class {{ structure.name }}
{{~ for member in structure.base_members ~}}
{{~ for line in member.comment ~}}
    # {{ line }}
{{~ end ~}}
    attr_accessor :{{ member.name }}
{{~ end ~}}
  end
{{~ for variant in structure.variants ~}}

  # One shape of +{{ structure.name }}+.
  #
  # The file carries +{{ variant.discriminator }}+ for it. That number rather than the name is
  # what lets this variant be renamed without a deployed reader reading a different one.
  class {{ variant.type_name }} < {{ structure.name }}
{{~ for member in variant.members ~}}
{{~ for line in member.comment ~}}
    # {{ line }}
{{~ end ~}}
    attr_accessor :{{ member.name }}
{{~ end ~}}
  end
{{~ end ~}}
{{ include 'ruby-file-foot.sbn' ~}}
